  "title": {
    "text": "Younger regions have more job churn, and they are also the denser ones",
    "subtitle": [
      "ITL2 regions: median age against job reallocation rate (jobs created + destroyed, % of employment), pooled 2011\u201324 (correlation -0.79).",
      "Colour = population density (population-weighted, log scale). Younger regions are much denser (correlation -0.89): dense, young cities churn most.",
      "Sources: ONS Longitudinal Business Database (Secure Access, SN 9501); ONS, NRS and NISRA population estimates; authors' calculations."
    ]
  },
